Raw spectra are corrected for detector acceptance, tracking inefficiency, hadronic interactions and resonance particle decays. The following subsections provide detailed overviews of these corrections.

Since detector parameters (gas pressure in the TPC, temperature) can change over the run, a minimum uncertainty (\(\sim 5\%\)) is assigned to the obtained correction factors. Errors on efficiencies are binomial and calculated as:

\[Err(p)=\sqrt{\frac{p(1-p)}{N}} \tag{6.3}\]

